WEBVTT

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:42.430
Oh, she's awake.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:43.740
So you did notice.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:47.040
Was the look in my eyes that intense?

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:51.050
Nah, I'd say my eyes are 
more intense than yours.

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:52.590
Check it out...

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:57.370
Uh, what? Is that different somehow?

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:01.500
Just look! My eyes are super intense!

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:05.970
Okay, I get it.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.010
So, good morning!

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:10.400
G-Good morning...

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.400
<b>Sakura, the Shrine, and the Zoo</b>

00:02:17.160 --> 00:02:19.150
Let's eat!

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.630
This is good!

00:02:35.630 --> 00:02:36.860
Glad to hear it!

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.290
For somethin' the brat made...

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.880
...it ain't bad.

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.310
It's disappearing pretty fast for 
something that's "not bad."

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:49.340
I wouldn't mind havin' seconds.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:50.020
Hmph.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.780
The chicken meatballs are good, too!

00:02:55.260 --> 00:02:57.550
Dad taught me how to make them.

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:59.770
We'll put them in the Chinese 
porridge, next time!

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.770
Yeah, in the brat's recipe.

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:06.150
As soon as we finish eating, 
we'll get ready to go.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:06.610
Yeah!

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.920
Everyone said they'd be there.

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:10.130
I can't wait!

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:11.970
I'm goin', too!

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:14.320
Make sure you stay in my bag.

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.090
And don't talk in your sleep.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.540
You can count on me!

00:03:21.610 --> 00:03:23.100
But first...

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.380
Picking up from last night!

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:16.560
<b>Tsukimine Shrine</b>

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:22.440
<b>Tsukimine Market</b>

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:20.280
I want cotton candy and a candy apple!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:22.430
I'm going to get baby castella cakes.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:25.540
So this is a Japanese shrine!

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:27.240
It's your first time seeing one?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.580
I've seen them in photos, but that's all.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.900
I wonder how Mizuki-sensei's doing...

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:36.330
She was our homeroom teacher 
in elementary school.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.250
She's in England, now.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.030
She's the daughter of the shrine's priest.

00:04:42.030 --> 00:04:43.370
I see.

00:04:43.370 --> 00:04:44.810
Speaking of shrines—

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.000
Hi, guys!

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.040
Meiling-chan! Sakura-chan!

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:48.750
Hello!

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:51.050
We're a little late...

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.510
Nah, you're fine.

00:04:59.020 --> 00:05:01.400
What a beautiful hairstyle!

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:07.110
M-Meiling-chan curled it for me.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:08.770
It's so cute!

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.730
It suits you!

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.010
Meiling-chan is amazing.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:17.570
I don't have curlers, so she just 
braided it and used tissues.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.860
It's too bad you didn't have hair spray,

00:05:20.860 --> 00:05:22.460
but it should last through the day.

00:05:22.790 --> 00:05:25.020
It came out great!

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:26.870
What's wrong?

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.810
It just feels like every time I try 
to talk lately, I get interrupted

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.680
by some great power.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.240
I hope that great power kicks in more often.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:38.930
Oh, right.

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:41.490
Li-kun will be a little late.

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.240
He said he'll let us know when 
he makes it to the shrine.

00:05:46.630 --> 00:05:47.760
You're right.

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:49.910
That's unusual for Syaoran...

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:53.110
He almost always shows up 
about ten minutes early.

00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:54.840
Yeah.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:06:00.320
Maybe he had something to do.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:01.720
Let's go on ahead.

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.010
Yeah.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:05.250
I'm the star today, anyway!

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:07.260
You never change, brat.

00:06:12.210 --> 00:06:15.840
So this is how a Japanese 
shrine market looks!

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:19.760
You said you've never visited 
a shrine on a market day,

00:06:19.760 --> 00:06:23.420
and Akiho-chan has never 
seen a shrine at all.

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:24.700
Right.

00:06:24.690 --> 00:06:35.790
<b>Tsukimine Market</b>

00:06:24.700 --> 00:06:28.370
I wasn't sure whether we should 
all go here or to the zoo.

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.960
But Yamazaki-kun looked up 
when the market day was,

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.460
and it turned out to be today.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.420
Thank you!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:35.790
You're welcome.

00:06:36.280 --> 00:06:39.900
I thought zoos would probably be 
about the same in any country.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:41.930
Anyway, speaking of shrines...

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:45.530
Drawing fortunes is always fun, too!

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:46.420
Drawing fortunes?

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:49.570
You pick a piece of paper, 
and it tells your fortune.

00:06:49.570 --> 00:06:50.760
I'd like to try that!

00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:54.010
I would've liked us to have 
gone to the zoo, too.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.360
Next time!

00:06:56.710 --> 00:06:58.580
<i>The zoo, huh?</i>

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.250
<i>Come to think of it, what was 
that all about yesterday?</i>

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:05.540
You know, the first character 
in the word for "shrine"...

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:08.210
<i>Meiling-chan looked like a cat, but I 
wonder what the others would be.</i>

00:07:05.540 --> 00:07:07.260
I can't hear you!

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:09.740
I said, the first character in "shrine"...

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:11.200
<i>I guess there aren't cats at the zoo, though.</i>

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.200
I can't hear you!

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:12.150
No, really, shrines...

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.330
<b>What?</b>

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:15.320
N-Nothing!

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:22.970
They really do sell all kinds of things here!

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.220
They used to mostly have antiques,

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:29.720
but recently, they've started selling 
sweets and tableware, too.

00:07:30.490 --> 00:07:31.630
These are cute!

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:35.140
<b>Cookie Shop</b>

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.200
They have lots of different shapes.

00:07:34.200 --> 00:07:37.140
Oh, look... Doesn't this one 
look like Momo-chan?

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.540
It does!

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:40.840
I'd like these!

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:44.330
All right. They're 100 yen each.

00:07:44.900 --> 00:07:46.180
Thank you.

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:50.790
Here.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:51.810
Huh?

00:07:51.810 --> 00:07:53.010
A gift.

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.190
But... But...

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:56.190
Take them. Okay?

00:07:59.150 --> 00:08:00.660
I'll treasure them!

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:03.180
I'd rather you ate them.

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:07.230
This is nice!

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:08.910
It really is.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:11.040
I could use it to hold pickled vegetables.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:15.390
Naoko-chan works with rice bran 
that's used to pickle foods.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.810
Rice bran?

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:19.960
I know what that is. 
It's full of enzymes, right?

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.780
I wonder what it tastes like.

00:08:22.170 --> 00:08:24.570
You don't eat the rice bran itself.

00:08:24.570 --> 00:08:26.870
You pickle different foods in it.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:28.020
I see!

00:08:28.540 --> 00:08:31.950
The best thing to put in rice 
bran is a helicopter.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.570
Each year, NASA—

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.730
Look! A helicopter!

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:49.740
Sorry I'm late!

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:51.640
No problem!

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.390
Did you finish what you needed to?

00:08:53.390 --> 00:08:55.350
Yeah, that's done.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:17.580
Bridges are actually made from chopsticks.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.140
So you went to that pancake place?

00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:19.290
It's what you call "recycling."

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:21.370
Yeah! The pancakes were so fluffy and good!

00:09:19.290 --> 00:09:23.710
It takes about 500,000 chopsticks 
to make a bridge ten meters long.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:22.870
Let's all go together, sometime!

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.050
Isn't the café au lait delicious?

00:09:26.050 --> 00:09:28.370
It is. I even bought the coffee beans.

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:30.620
A gift for Kaito-san?

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:32.580
Yes.

00:09:32.850 --> 00:09:34.800
You and he came to Japan together, right?

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:36.420
Y-Yes.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:40.150
You don't have to be so nervous. 
I won't eat you.

00:09:40.150 --> 00:09:42.260
No, she'll totally eat you.

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.880
Hasn't it been hard on you?

00:09:44.880 --> 00:09:47.730
Well, I have someone to help me.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.820
Um, what about you, Li-san?

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:51.020
Just call me Meiling!

00:09:52.390 --> 00:09:55.530
Meiling-san, how was it 
when you lived in Japan?

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.380
I had someone to take care of me, too.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.540
Are you used to Japan yet?

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:03.310
I still get confused sometimes,

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:05.500
but everyone I know here is very nice.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:08.880
Yeah, there are definitely 
a lot of pushovers here.

00:10:09.280 --> 00:10:11.880
And they don't even realize it themselves!

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:16.000
I guess birds of a feather do flock together.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.750
You shouldn't rub your eyes.

00:10:27.750 --> 00:10:29.180
R-Right...

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.090
Is something wrong, Sakura-san?

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.200
Uh...

00:10:44.230 --> 00:10:45.840
What's the matter?

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:46.910
Um...

00:10:47.080 --> 00:10:48.900
Done with your drinks?

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:49.740
Yes!

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:51.030
Ready to move on?

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:55.710
What's wrong?

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:57.000
Sakura-chan?

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:58.250
Is something going on?

00:10:58.250 --> 00:11:00.420
Y-You guys... Your ears... Your ears!

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:01.280
Ears?

00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:02.580
Did you buy them at a stall?

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.670
Were they even selling animal ears?

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:07.250
Tails? You bought tails, too?!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:11.080
What's wrong with you, Kinomoto-san? 
What is it <i>meow</i>?

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:11.890
Meow?

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:13.860
Did something <i>baa-aaa</i>-ad happen?

00:11:13.860 --> 00:11:14.750
Baa?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.180
What is <i>boing</i> on?

00:11:16.180 --> 00:11:16.630
Boing?

00:11:16.630 --> 00:11:17.960
There's something <i>arf</i> about you.

00:11:17.960 --> 00:11:18.400
Arf?

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.160
You don't seem <i>bear</i>y well.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:30.150
What happened?

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:38.960
Everyone has animal ears and tails!

00:11:40.130 --> 00:11:41.830
Ears and tails?

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:21.490
What's going on?

00:12:21.950 --> 00:12:23.490
Where is everyone?

00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:25.540
Syaoran-kun?

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.120
What the heck is this?!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.150
Kero-chan!

00:12:33.560 --> 00:12:36.540
What is this place? When did 
we leave the shrine?

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:37.860
We didn't!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:41.370
I saw animal ears and tails on everyone, 
and then, suddenly...

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.650
Meow!

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:50.110
What the heck?!

00:12:50.110 --> 00:12:51.990
This is no time to play around!

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:54.540
Sorry, it's a gut reaction 
when things get weird.

00:12:55.790 --> 00:12:57.670
But seriously, what's goin' on?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.420
I don't know...

00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:02.610
Well, it's gotta be the work of a 
you-know-what. Right, Sakura?

00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:03.470
Yeah.

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.970
<i>Key that hides the forces of dreams.</i>

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:13.450
<i>Show me your true form!</i>

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:16.750
<i>Release!</i>

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:41.140
Why animals? And what is this place?

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:44.930
I think they're both because of a new card...

00:13:44.930 --> 00:13:48.330
Can you sense it coming from a 
specific spot? Do you feel anything?

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:49.140
I'll try.

00:13:54.840 --> 00:13:58.220
I-It seems like it's coming 
from this entire area.

00:13:58.220 --> 00:13:59.870
The entire area?

00:13:59.870 --> 00:14:03.580
It's not just in one spot. It's all around.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:06.290
So how are we supposed 
to turn it into a card?

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:09.010
What about your friends, out there?

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:10.590
It's not them.

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:13.490
But why are they turning into animals?

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.610
They're kind of cute.

00:14:15.610 --> 00:14:18.040
But still... I have to...

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:18.840
Huh?

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:19.870
Wh-What is it?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:25.460
Is it me, or do they look even more like 
animals than they did a minute ago?

00:14:31.340 --> 00:14:33.850
They basically <i>are</i> animals, now!

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:35.470
We have to do something, fast!

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.510
Right.

00:14:49.740 --> 00:14:50.660
Wait!

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:08.300
What do I do? What if they never turn back?

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.460
Sakura!

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.990
What's goin' on?

00:15:17.030 --> 00:15:18.050
What now?

00:15:52.760 --> 00:15:54.080
What's happening?

00:15:55.130 --> 00:15:56.210
Kero-chan?

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:20.490
I used magic... to stop time.

00:16:20.490 --> 00:16:21.300
Huh?

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:26.290
With my magical power, it won't last long.

00:16:26.900 --> 00:16:28.410
You have to find the cause.

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:32.400
I can't find it. The feeling is 
coming from all around...

00:16:32.900 --> 00:16:35.840
Didn't you say something about animal ears?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:38.270
Does that bring anything to mind?

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:42.810
It can be anything, no matter how small.

00:16:43.740 --> 00:16:48.720
I wasn't sure... whether to go to 
the shrine or the zoo, today.

00:16:49.670 --> 00:16:52.800
I was thinking I would've liked to 
have gone to the zoo, too...

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:53.970
And?

00:16:54.270 --> 00:16:59.880
And... the next thing I knew, 
I was surrounded by grasslands.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:03.050
And everyone looked like animals.

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.950
They started looking more and 
more like actual animals!

00:17:06.950 --> 00:17:09.290
I don't know what to do!

00:17:10.690 --> 00:17:13.230
I... I...

00:17:22.010 --> 00:17:23.840
Syaoran-kun...

00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:27.440
It's okay. I'm here.

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:34.620
Are you still scared?

00:17:38.460 --> 00:17:40.620
Can you take a deep breath?

00:17:47.640 --> 00:17:50.600
My magic's effect will soon wear off...

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:52.700
You have to think.

00:17:53.120 --> 00:17:54.540
What do you want to happen?

00:17:55.610 --> 00:17:59.500
I want everyone... to go back to normal.

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:03.270
I want everyone... to go 
back to our own world.

00:18:06.820 --> 00:18:12.580
Then, wish hard for that, Sakura...

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:21.950
Sakura?

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:30.840
I want everyone to go back to normal.

00:18:31.390 --> 00:18:33.700
I want everyone to go back to our own world.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.410
<i>With Syaoran-kun!</i>

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:26.420
<i>Force without master,</i>

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:30.090
<i>heed the call of my Staff of Dreams, 
and become my power!</i>

00:19:30.090 --> 00:19:31.050
<i>Secure!</i>

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:44.660
<b>Mirage</b>

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:48.490
Syaoran-kun! Kero-chan!

00:19:55.240 --> 00:19:58.140
That really scared me. 
You suddenly disappeared...

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:59.930
Did something happen?

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:04.150
I asked them to go check out the 
other side of the shrine for me.

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:07.440
Is Li-kun okay?

00:20:07.440 --> 00:20:10.130
I think the forest air just got to him.

00:20:07.700 --> 00:20:10.670
Li-kun, would you like some more water?

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:12.720
I'll go buy some.

00:20:15.140 --> 00:20:16.570
I'll go with you!

00:20:19.340 --> 00:20:23.530
So that's what made Li-kun feel ill.

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:27.110
He overtaxed himself, 
stopping time with his magic.

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:32.920
Are you doing okay, Kero-chan?

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:38.920
I just lost consciousness when 
we came back to our world.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:41.720
Talk about pathetic...

00:20:41.720 --> 00:20:44.130
Ya don't have to worry 'bout me, Sakura!

00:20:45.880 --> 00:20:47.420
Thanks.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:52.010
But it was my fault.

00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:58.550
Your parents said that you'd pushed 
yourself way too hard in training.

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:00.280
Still not enough?

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.200
No.

00:21:03.490 --> 00:21:06.460
And you're doing it for Kinomoto-san, right?

00:21:06.910 --> 00:21:09.620
I'm really aggravated, right now!

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.530
Because I don't have magic myself.

00:21:14.280 --> 00:21:19.510
Even without magic, you've been 
plenty of help to Sakura and me.

00:21:25.300 --> 00:21:26.470
What?

00:21:29.640 --> 00:21:31.600
You call her "Sakura," huh?

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:35.650
Oh, it's fine. Don't get all worked up.

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:37.610
You'll make yourself sick again!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:42.860
By the way, did you tell Kinomoto-san 
what you thought of her hair?

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.990
<b>Mirage</b>

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:47.620
"Mirage"...

00:21:48.960 --> 00:21:50.380
Mirage.

00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:57.320
The things I was thinking about 
became reality because of this card.

00:21:57.960 --> 00:22:02.080
When I got scared, it made 
things even scarier.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:05.770
Syaoran-kun stopped all of that.

00:22:05.770 --> 00:22:09.140
I know he pushed himself too hard.

00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:12.500
Stopping time is really advanced magic.

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:17.590
I'm sure anyone in the Li family would 
know lots of spells and techniques,

00:22:17.590 --> 00:22:19.930
but when it comes to actually using them...

00:22:19.930 --> 00:22:21.770
It can't be easy.

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:29.370
More new cards might cause even 
more things like this to happen.

00:22:30.250 --> 00:22:35.660
So, to make sure no one has to get 
hurt or scared when that happens,

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:38.830
I want to get stronger.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:12.230
Hidey-howdy-ho!

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:12.970
<b>Leave It to Kero-chan!</b>

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:15.330
Are y'all resting when ya get the chance?

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:21.230
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:12.970 --> 00:24:21.230
<b>K</b>

00:24:15.330 --> 00:24:17.480
Good things come to those who wait. 
Time for "Leave It to Kero-chan!"

00:24:17.480 --> 00:24:21.230
Today, I'm introducin' Sakura's school, 
Tomoeda Middle School!

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:23.690
It's a stylish building, with a canal 
that flows past the front gate.

00:24:23.690 --> 00:24:26.050
The classrooms have high 
ceilings to promote study.

00:24:26.050 --> 00:24:28.430
The blackboards curve around, 
to be visible from the sides.

00:24:28.430 --> 00:24:31.150
This is the back courtyard. Under the arch 
is the perfect spot for sharin' secrets.

00:24:31.150 --> 00:24:33.680
Whoever cares for the white 
roses gives 'em lots of love!

00:24:32.200 --> 00:24:33.200
<b>Can you write the kanji for "rose"?</b>

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>Bear      Cat</b>

00:24:33.200 --> 00:24:37.280
<b>K</b>

00:24:33.680 --> 00:24:37.090
The kid showed up, right when Sakura 
needed help. He ain't always so bad!

00:24:37.090 --> 00:24:38.370
I won't lose, next time!

00:24:38.370 --> 00:24:39.990
Ta-ta!

00:24:40.000 --> 00:24:42.250
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:24:40.340 --> 00:24:43.390
I wonder what Tomoyo-chan wants to show me.

00:24:43.390 --> 00:24:45.790
Wait, is this play the one where...

00:24:46.900 --> 00:24:49.130
This is too embarrassing!

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:51.930
Next time, "Sakura's Nostalgic Viewing Party."

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:55.010
<b>Sakura's Nostalgic Viewing Party</b>

00:24:51.930 --> 00:24:55.010
Say it with me: "Release!"

00:24:55.010 --> 00:25:00.010
<b>End</b>
